course: dictionary
lesson: 4729
title: Horizon: near, far and beyond
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A horizon is the line far away where the land or sea seems to meet the sky. Context helps you find its meaning. «Turtle hatchlings climb out of their nests at night and head for the brightest horizon, usually the sea.» The clue is usually the sea: the horizon is the place where the sea seems to meet the sky.
explain: Horizon can also mean the limit of what you know and have seen. The Rat in the story only knew the hills near him, so they were his «simple horizon». To broaden your horizons means to learn and see new things, so your world gets bigger.
explain: Watch for phrases. «On the horizon» does not mean on a line in the sky. It means likely to happen soon. If you can say the phrase in your own words and it still fits the sentence, your meaning is right.
fact: A horizon is the line far away where the land or sea seems to meet the sky.
fact: Your horizons are the limits of what you know and have experienced.
fact: «On the horizon» means likely to happen soon.
fact: The Earth is round, which is why ships disappear bottom first over the horizon.
fact: «Horizontal» means flat, like the horizon, and comes from this word.
exercise: «Turtle hatchlings climb out of their nests at night and head for the brightest horizon, usually the sea.» Where do the hatchlings head? | *The sea, where it meets the sky | A dark forest | Their nests | The hotel roof
exercise: Mia says, «Our class wants to broaden our horizons this year.» What does broaden your horizons mean? | To forget what you already know | To make the classroom bigger | *To learn and see new things | To draw a straight line on paper
exercise: «The Moon looks bigger near the horizon, but a coin held at arm's length shows it is the same size.» What does horizontal mean? | Standing straight up | *Flat, like the horizon | Round like a ball | Very far away
test: «Soil has layers called horizons: dark topsoil, paler subsoil below, and broken rock above the bedrock.» In this sentence, what are the horizons? | Kinds of plants | Holes dug by worms | Lines drawn in the sky | *Layers of soil
test: Why do ships disappear bottom first over the horizon? | Because the Sun gets in the way | *Because the Earth is round | Because ships sink quickly | Because the sea is flat
exam: What does «on the horizon» mean? | Hidden inside a box | *Likely to happen soon | Far under the sea | Very flat and grey
